   "captions_sha256": "5c3e4350afa44378a380410fba3d7537ff5d5826c6d3f1aa9afe912caa916c54",
   "created_at": "2026-11-24T03:49:14Z",
   "description": "NASA chased the Moon's shadow at 50,000 feet during the August 12, 2026 total solar eclipse. Clouds covered Iceland, so a NASA WB-57 jet flew above them, racing the eclipse to film the Sun's corona. Here is how the flight worked, and what its cameras saw.\n\nIn this episode:\n0:00 Clouds over Iceland on eclipse day\n0:20 The mystery of the corona\n0:34 A research jet from Houston\n0:48 Racing the shadow\n1:00 Why fly at 50,000 feet\n1:14 Takeoff from Keflavik\n1:25 Inside totality\n1:48 Balloons below\n1:59 What the team got\n\nSources:\n- NASA, \"NASA Johnson Pilots Chase Moon's Shadow for Eclipse Science\" (Aug 26, 2026): https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/nasa-johnson-pilots-chase-moons-shadow-for-eclipse-science/\n- NASA, \"NASA Shares Views of August Solar Eclipse from Ground, Air, Space\" (Aug 21, 2026): https://science.nasa.gov/science-research/heliophysics/nasa-shares-views-of-august-solar-eclipse-from-ground-air-space/\n- NASA, \"NASA Science Soars During August Total Solar Eclipse\" (Jul 27, 2026): https://science.nasa.gov/science-research/heliophysics/nasa-science-soars-during-august-total-solar-eclipse/\n\nFootage: NASA via the Scientific Visualization Studio: https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/15075 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/15065 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/15063 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5656 . Public domain; NASA does not endorse this video. The colour corona panels are from the WB-57's 2024 eclipse flight (NASA/SwRI/Will Ashfield) and the balloon shots are from earlier US eclipses (labelled on screen). Eclipse path views are NASA visualizations. Charts: Orbital Atlas.\nNarration: the channel creator's own voice, generated with ElevenLabs voice cloning.\n\n#SolarEclipse #NASA #Iceland #OrbitalAtlas",
